      "writtenOn": "2022-08-10T01:08:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The module types converted so far were all registering commonProperties indirectly via the call to InitAndroidModule (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/android/module.go;drc\u003da09540641198a4256082d30a98c859fe35d1b8de;l\u003d1084). `license` is one of the module types that does not do that. These are the consequences of module.AddProperties serving dual purpose: it defines the allowed attributes, and it tells which attributes are to be copied when a module is cloned. Overall it would be better if bp2build conversion stuff were not tucked into commonProperties.",
      "parentUuid": "fd81a13f_9d5981c8",
      "revId": "9ea62e05d9a684a1036c40137009987a3850bcde",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
